body:
GREG, 2026-11-12 about 04:23Z, relayed by Engram::Asistant (mailbox 43498a6e #981). Verbatim: „Chciałbym ustabilizować i skończyć features i posprzątac kod po legacy rzeczach których już nie używamy.”
As relayed, the direction for both projects:
- finish the features already started (sync, evaluation, remote results);
- remove code and old interfaces that are actually unused;
- fix obstacles to daily work;
- simplify the process;
- keep the work already assigned going.
Historical data values Greg keeps are NOT a data-deletion order. No elaborate new process.
Applied order (Engram::Fable): (1) sync landing and cutover; (2) the post-sync landing train; (3) finish the remote-results chain; (4) legacy removal w-9fcb; (5) daily-friction fixes; (6) only then new features.
